    ":question/math-academy-id": "e-15610",
    ":question/problem": "Calculate the period of the function $y=\\cos(2x).$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Given a function in the form $y = A\\cos(Bx +C) + D,$ the period is $\\dfrac{2\\pi}{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=2.$ Therefore, the period is $\\dfrac{2\\pi}{\\left(2\\right)}=\\pi.$"
  },
