      ":question/problem": "Calculate the period of the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Given a function in the form $f(x)=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period $T$ is given by $\\frac{2\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=\\frac{5}{3}.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{(\\frac{5}{3})}=\\frac{6\\pi }{5}.$"
