      ":question/problem": "Calculate the period of the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}(12x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Given a function in the form $y=A\\operatorname{cos}(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=12.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{12}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$"
